The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
// Omission of the include directive
// vsc7514_regs.h file does not include <soc/mscc/ocelot_vcap.h>
extern const u32 vsc7514_ana_regmap[];
extern const u32 vsc7514_qs_regmap[];
```
Reason:
The absence of the include directive for `<soc/mscc/ocelot_vcap.h>` in the `vsc7514_regs.h` file resulted in unresolved dependencies for the definitions that rely on the contents of `ocelot_vcap.h`, leading to compilation errors.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#include <soc/mscc/ocelot_vcap.h>
```
Reason:
Adding the include directive for `<soc/mscc/ocelot_vcap.h>` in the `vsc7514_regs.h` file resolves the unresolved dependencies by ensuring that the necessary definitions from `ocelot_vcap.h` are available, thus allowing the code to compile successfully.

